// What: a style's text from a value (prerendered, it could close the style and start markup)
// Expect: a style's text is unescaped in HTML (a value could close it), so Wutu writes it only as written: style { "…"; }
using Browser from std:Browser;

fn view(css: Str) Browser.HTMLElement {
    @wutu/\
    div {
        style { = css; }
    }
    \/;
}

export main() void {
    Browser.document.body.append(view("p { color: red; }"));
}
